WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.901
-I miss you.
I'm so happy you're back.

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.501
Welcome back.
Thanks for being here.

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:06.200
-Thanks for having me.
Hello, everyone.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.934
Hi. Hi.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:10.000
-You're back.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.334
"Saturday Night Live"
this weekend.

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:13.767
But before we get into that,
I want to talk about --

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:15.067
you were at The White House.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.501
-I was. Oh, my gosh.

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:20.400
-On the day that they passed
the Respect for Marriage Act.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:27.234
And that is a massive moment
for this country.

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:28.434
What was it like?

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:29.634
What was it like
getting the call?

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:31.367
What was it like getting there?
Who did you see?

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:32.634
What happened?
-It was wild.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:34.868
We got an e-mail from
The White House that said,

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:35.934
"From The White House."

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:37.501
-From The White House. Yeah.

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:38.567
That right there is enough.
You go, "What?!"

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:39.968
-It was mad.

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:41.868
And I just never thought --
I mean, I'm British, right?

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:44.667
So I never thought I would be
in that place singing.

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:47.467
And it was such a beautiful day,
such a beautiful step

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:49.501
in the right direction
for our community,

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:51.868
and I was just very honored.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:55.767
-You sang "Stay With Me,"
which I love,

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.234
but you changed
some of the lyrics.

00:00:57.234 --> 00:00:59.300
-Yeah, I did.
-What lyrics did you change?

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.934
-Well, it's, like, a lonely song
about one-night stands,

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:03.267
so I decided --

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:04.868
[ Laughter ]
-Is it?

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:06.400
-Yeah, it is.
It's pretty depressing.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.968
So, I --
-I always sing it happy.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.567
-But I changed it to, like,
be a love song,

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:12.901
and it was really beautiful.

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:15.334
And there's certain lyrics
I'm going to keep forever.

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:16.968
-What was the president like?
How was the vice president?

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:18.634
-Oh, stunning.
-He's great?

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:20.100
-He's fabulous.
They're all great.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.701
Kamala loved my handbag,
which I was very happy with.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:24.734
-Yes!

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:25.734
We have a picture
with you guys there,

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:26.834
all of you together.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.667
-They were very sweet
and kind to me

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:31.167
and my team and everyone.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.501
Like, my band loved them.
It was a beautiful day.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:36.200
-Do you get star-struck at all
in your career anymore?

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.767
-I do, I do.
With the pop divas.

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:39.767
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.100
-Really?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.300
Like, if I see Rihanna or
Madonna, I fall to the floor.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.367
-Really? To this day?
-Oh, my God, of course.

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:47.634
-I read somewhere, by the way,

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:50.334
that Lady Gaga once got you
in a little trouble.

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:56.434
-Yeah, I skipped school to see
her "Monster Ball Tour,"

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:59.501
and I, like,
forged a letter from my dad.

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:02.534
And then I got put in detention
for like a week afterwards.

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:03.567
It was crazy.
-You got busted.

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:06.234
-I was a bad liar.
Bad, bad liar.

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:07.601
-Does Gaga know
she got you in trouble?

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:10.100
-I don't think she knows this,
but it was so worth it.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:14.000
It was so worth it.
-And look at you now.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.334
Your new album, "Gloria."

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:18.801
This is your
fourth studio album.

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.968
I love the name, "Gloria."

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:22.634
My sister's name is Gloria.

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:24.133
My mother's name is Gloria.
-I love that.

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.501
-My grandmother's name
is Gloria.

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:28.434
-Best name in the world.
-How unoriginal is my family?

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:30.300
You can't think of another name?

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.234
My dad's name was Jim.
I was Jim.

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:33.701
So it's really unoriginal.

00:02:33.701 --> 00:02:35.834
They go, "Yeah, we'll have kids.
We'll name them Jim and Gloria."

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:37.701
-Two great names.
-But I love "Gloria."

00:02:37.701 --> 00:02:39.467
This is fantastic.

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:42.400
"Gloria" isn't based on a person
that you know, necessarily.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.434
-No. It's a word that's meant
a lot to me throughout my life.

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:47.567
And, you know, the
Laura Branigan

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:50.801
gay anthem "Gloria" is something
I've always heard in gay clubs.

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:55.033
And then "Gloria" in school,
through singing hymns and stuff.

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:57.601
But for me, "Gloria"
is something that I've called

00:02:57.601 --> 00:03:02.000
a spirit inside of me that says
to me, "You keep going.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.434
You've got this. Carry on."

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:05.100
It's like a fighter spirit
within me.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.467
-Yeah, I love that.
-I've called it "Gloria."

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:09.033
I love that. That's great.

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:11.968
I heard -- You know I'm a fan.

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:13.834
But when "Unholy" came out,
I was like --

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.501
Oh, I was just hoping
it was great.

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:16.634
And it's beyond great.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:19.667
It was like...
[ Vocalizes ]

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:21.300
Like, "Oh, my gosh!"

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.000
You got a banger here, bud.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.267
And I never say
the word "banger."

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:26.434
And it was unbelievable.

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:29.067
And now "Gimme"
is another super-smash.

00:03:29.067 --> 00:03:30.234
I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:32.834
You got Jessie Reyez
on there and Koffee.

00:03:32.834 --> 00:03:36.701
And, so, now,
before the album comes out,

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:37.934
is there
any more releases or no?

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:40.400
-There's one more song, yeah.
One more song.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.267
And, like, amazing.
There's a video, everything.

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:46.901
I explode into glitter.
-You don't have to say it.

00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:48.334
-This one.
-Okay, yeah.

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:49.434
-Yeah.
-Wow!

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:51.534
-Yeah, it's --
[ Laughs ]

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:53.334
-I'm excited about this.
-It's going to be fun.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:55.234
-You're doing
"Saturday Night Live."

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:56.234
I think you might have
been here the first time

00:03:56.234 --> 00:03:57.334
you did "Saturday Night Live."

00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:59.467
It was eight years ago.
-Yeah, it's wild.

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:00.634
-Different time.

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:02.067
-Different time.
I'm not as nervous.

00:04:02.067 --> 00:04:05.100
I was [bleep]
myself the first time.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.634
But it's nice now.
It's, like, a nice feeling.

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:09.868
I feel -- It's the fourth time
I've been there,

00:04:09.868 --> 00:04:11.300
so I'm a bit more calm.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.367
-What was it like after doing
the first "Saturday Night Live"?

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:15.300
Were you --
-I mean, it changed my life.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:19.000
That night after doing it was --
It changed my career.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.133
It's like, I feel like people
knew who I was after that show,

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:23.300
so it was crazy.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.567
-Coming from England,
I mean, does that --

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:28.100
Do you go,
"Oh, America is the goal"?

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.601
-Oh, my God, always.
-Really?

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:30.968
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:33.033
I always wanted to be -- Yeah.
It's my dream.

00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:34.968
-And the next day, Sunday,
you're walking down the streets,

00:04:34.968 --> 00:04:36.334
and everyone's like,
"You're Sam Smith."

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:37.767
-Yeah, New Yorkers
knew who I was.

00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:39.133
I was -- My dream was made.

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:41.167
-Yeah, that's exactly
what I'm talking about.

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:45.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.400
The tour --
When does the tour start?

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.200
-April.
-The tour starts in April.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:52.300
Okay. The album comes out not
this Friday, next Friday,

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.400
and then tour in April.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:54.667
Are you ready for the tour?

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:55.734
-Yeah, it's going to be --
You all have to come.

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:56.968
It's going to be stunning.

00:04:56.968 --> 00:04:59.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
It will be great.

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:01.567
-You're actually coming back to
New York in August.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.501
I want to say
August 8th and 9th.

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:05.234
-Madison Square Garden.
-Madison Square Garden.

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:06.634
-Yeah.
-I will be there.

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:08.000
I will be there cheering you on.
-Please.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.534
-I love you.
Sam Smith, everybody.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:12.968
Their album, "Gloria,"
is out next Friday.

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:16.334
You can see Sam this weekend on
"Saturday Night Live."

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:17.534
We'll be right back
with more "Tonight Show."

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:18.634
Come on back.

